exit 0
Usage: werk <verb> [arguments] [flags]

A card id may start with one #: #auth and auth name the same card.

Verbs:

  accept <id>
      Accept one ghost, with its ghost parents, options and evidence, or a pending change. Only the person accepts.
      --actor <text>  you: the person asked for this accept.

  add <id>
      Propose a card, an option or a source as a ghost. The person accepts it in the map.
      --title <text>    The title: one sentence about the node's own rule.
      --why <text>      Why the node holds.
      --body <text>     The details.
      --parent <id>     The card it refines. A card defaults to the root.
      --kind <text>     card (the default), option or source.
      --status <text>   open (the default) or proto.
      --who <text>      Who decides: you, me or prototype.
      --why_not <text>  For an option: why it lost.
      --url <text>      For a source: where it is.
      --finding <text>  For a source: what it found.

  discard <id>
      Drop one ghost, with its ghost descendants and the evidence that only they cite, or a pending change.

  edit <id>
      Set who decides a card, or waive its basis or its option with a written reason.
      --who <text>           Who decides: you, me or prototype.
      --no-basis <text>      Why no decided card is a basis of this card.
      --unchallenged <text>  Why no option was weighed against this card.

  find [<id>]
      List the open and proto cards under a card, breadth first, or in the whole map, without the paused, stale and postponed ones.

  help
      Print every verb with its arguments and flags.

  inbox
      Print the notes typed in the map, in log order.
      --since <text>  Start after this log position.
      -n <text>       Print at most this many notes (default 20).

  kill <id>
      Record one kill criterion on a card: what must become true to revisit the decision.
      --metric <text>     The metric to track. Needs --source, --threshold and --window.
      --source <text>     Where the metric comes from.
      --threshold <text>  The value that fires the criterion.
      --window <text>     The time window the metric is read over.
      --manual <text>     The test the author runs by hand.
      --no-metric <text>  Why no metric applies.
      --revisit           Revisit at any time.

  link <from> <to>
      Add one typed link from one node to another. A depends_on link needs --why.
      --type <text>  refines, depends_on, supported_by or alternative_to.
      --why <text>   For depends_on: what <from> takes from <to>.

  propose <id>
      Stage a change to a node's title, why or body. The person accepts it in the map.
      --title <text>   The new title.
      --why <text>     The new why.
      --ops <text>     The body as a JSON list of ops: {"tag":"elaborated","old","new"}, {"tag":"new","new"} or {"tag":"removed","old"}. Every block of the body is the old of one op.
      --review <text>  On a decided card: the sentence that ends its review in an amend. The trace of each card the amend marks shows it.

  quote <card> <conversation> [<text>]
      Quote the words of one spoken message of a conversation as an excerpt that supports a card.
      --text <text>  The words to quote, exactly as they were said.

  rederive <id>
      Confirm a stale card unchanged and clear its stale marks. An amend goes through werk propose instead.
      --confirm <text>  The depends_on targets whose link reasons you read and confirm, separated by commas.
      --status <text>   decided: also decide the card, through the contract check.

  remove <id>
      Take a card out of the map with its subtree, or with --reparent only the card. Only the person removes.
      --actor <text>  you: the person asked for this.
      --reparent      Move the card's direct children up to its parent.

  removed
      List each removal: the card it named, and every node it took out.

  reopen <id>
      Reopen a decided card. Invalidated and rejected mark the next hop stale; postponed pauses every card downstream.
      --reason <text>  postponed, invalidated or rejected. The default is invalidated.
      --why <text>     The text that the trace of each marked card shows.

  restore <id>
      Undo the removal that named a card: the card and all it took come back. Only the person restores.
      --actor <text>  you: the person asked for this.

  say <id> <text>
      Write one note on the thread of a card. The map shows it on the card.

  search [<term>] ...
      With no term, print the id and title of every decided card. With terms, print the cards whose words hold every term, the most hits first.
      --status <text>  decided, open or proto: keep the cards with that status only.
      --under <id>     Keep the refines subtree of this card only.

  serve
      Start the map in the browser, on the loopback address.
      --port <text>  The port (default 4000). 0 takes any free port.

  show [<id>]
      Print one node, or the root card when no id is given: its rollup, links and marks, and the words of its options, excerpts and sources.

  stale [<id>]
      List the stale, paused and waiting cards, a basis before the card on it, each with the reason of its mark.
      --kind <text>  stale, paused or waiting: list one kind of mark only.

  status <id> <status>
      Decide a card. The contract check needs who, a basis, an option and a kill criterion.

  ticket-check <folder>
      Check a folder of tickets: the own checks on each ticket, then the set checks. Exit 0 pass, 1 fail, 2 malformed call.
      --root <id>    The card whose decided subtree the tickets must cite
      --spec <text>  The spec whose User stories the tickets must deliver

  unlink <from> <to>
      Remove one typed link from the map. The log keeps it.
      --type <text>  refines, depends_on, supported_by or alternative_to.
